The Dispose method disposes the internal HttpClient only if it was created internally (not passed in). The HttpClientProvider.GetHttpClient(httpClient) method is used to get the HttpClient instance, which might return the passed-in client or create a new one.

To test Dispose, we want to verify that Dispose is called on the HttpClient only if it was created internally. Since HttpClient.Dispose is not virtual, we cannot mock it directly. Instead, we can create a derived class of HttpClient that overrides Dispose and sets a flag. Then we pass that derived class instance to the HuggingFaceEmbeddingGenerator constructor and verify the flag after Dispose is called.

I will create a test file with two tests:
- Dispose_InternalHttpClient_DisposesHttpClient: create HuggingFaceEmbeddingGenerator with null HttpClient (so it creates its own), then call Dispose and verify the derived HttpClient's Dispose was called.
- Dispose_ExternalHttpClient_DoesNotDisposeHttpClient: create HuggingFaceEmbeddingGenerator with an external HttpClient (our derived class), call Dispose and verify Dispose was not called on the external client.

I will submit this test now.

